      "content": "# The dsh-trading bundle: stacked on top of the stock `web` (or `headless`)\n# profile. One row per plugin; users patch rows by id from their profile's\n# cordis.patch.yml — e.g. replace `market-data-provider`'s config to point\n# `root` at their own candle store, or swap the row wholesale for their own\n# provider package. That row swap IS the bring-your-own-data mechanism.\n\n- insert:\n    - id: market-data\n      name: '@dsh-trading/market-data'\n\n    - id: market-data-provider\n      name: '@dsh-trading/provider-csv'\n      config:\n        root: ./data\n\n    - id: tool-market\n      name: '@dsh-trading/tool-market'\n      config:\n        chartDir: ./charts\n\n    # The evaluation harness: audit_backtest / lint_strategy_code judge\n    # backtest artifacts against real candles — deterministic checks whose\n    # verdict is allowed to be NOT PROVEN.\n    - id: verdict\n      name: '@dsh-trading/verdict'\n\n    # Refuses order-execution and fund-movement tool names from ANY plugin in\n    # this profile, not just ours. Remove this row to opt out deliberately.\n    - id: risk-guard\n      name: '@dsh-trading/risk-guard'\n\n    # Candlestick cards for market_snapshot / get_ohlcv results, plus the\n    # persistent chart column and the loopback channel that feeds it. Those\n    # are web-only; under a headless profile the row still registers\n    # `get_chart_view` and the per-turn context line, which simply report a\n    # closed panel. Remove the row for the generic text cards.\n    - id: client-chart\n      name: '@dsh-trading/client-chart'\n"
